invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: each group XORs its sixteen rows of 16 bytes last to first. In
  place each 16 bytes are still read before they are written, so the
  output stays right there; with the output 5 bytes below the input, as
  rec_open decrypts over its header, the last row's write lands on the
  last 5 input bytes of the row before it before they are read.
  chacha20.h allows that shape, and bin/chacha20_equiv_test runs it at
  every length.

--- old
    for (size_t row = 0; row < 16; row++) {
--- new
    for (size_t row = 16; row-- > 0;) {
